{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-87827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $5\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}\\le 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x} & \\le 4 \\\\ {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x} & \\le \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bab10e2b325c4ae299c97bbdf0cb17f1f777c06a5d6805721f3ae622bb1110e2"} {"question" "q-87827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87827" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${(0.72)}^{x}-4\\le 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(0.72)}^{x}-4 & \\le 0 \\\\ {(0.72)}^{x} & \\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[(0.72)^{x}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72)$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bab10e2b325c4ae299c97bbdf0cb17f1f777c06a5d6805721f3ae622bb1110e2"} {"question" "q-87831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.70)}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72)}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72)}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.72)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $9\\cdot {6}^{x}\\ge {7}^{1-x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\cdot {6}^{x} & \\ge {7}^{1-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\cdot {6}^{x}) & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1-x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡9+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{x}) & \\ge (1-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡9+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6 & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡7-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7 & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7) & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bab10e2b325c4ae299c97bbdf0cb17f1f777c06a5d6805721f3ae622bb1110e2"} {"question" "q-87855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7+\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7+\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡9-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-{e}^{3x-2}>15.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{3x-2} & >15 \\\\ {e}^{3x-2} & <-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{e}^{3x-2}>0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality ${e}^{3x-2}<-15$ has no solutions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bab10e2b325c4ae299c97bbdf0cb17f1f777c06a5d6805721f3ae622bb1110e2"} {"question" "q-87873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<\\frac{1}{15}"] ["math" "x<\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "x>\\frac{2}{15}"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solutions"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-87873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "no solutions"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-277888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{3-4x}<{8}^{3-x}.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\,<\\,\\infty $" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-277888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${8}^{3-x}$ is always positive and $-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{3-4x}$ is always negative, we always have\n\n$$\n-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{3-4x}<{8}^{3-x}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-\\infty <x<\\infty \n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-277888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bab10e2b325c4ae299c97bbdf0cb17f1f777c06a5d6805721f3ae622bb1110e2"} {"question" "q-277888" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b3f34d90956b4177e7913ec8fb"} {"question" "q-277888" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995013/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bb82ef5de31e31192c00aeef3568aedeeaa30b